# Chess Duel — Privacy Policy

**Effective date:** November 6, 2026  
**Last updated:** November 6, 2026

Chess Duel is a **free Android chess game with no advertisements**. This policy explains what information the app handles and how it is used.

## At a glance

- **No account required** — you can play without signing up or logging in.
- **No advertising or analytics** — the app does not include advertising SDKs or usage-tracking analytics.
- **Your game data stays on your device** — game progress and match history are stored locally.
- **No sensitive permissions** — the app does not require access to your camera, microphone, contacts, or location.

## 1. Information we collect

We do not collect or transmit personal information through Chess Duel. The app does not ask for your name, email address, phone number, contacts, or location. It does not use advertising identifiers, tracking pixels, or analytics tools to profile you or measure your activity.

## 2. Information stored on your device

Chess Duel is designed for offline, local play. Game progress, match history, board positions, and chess-clock state are stored on your device for the app's features. We do not upload this information to our servers or provide cloud synchronization.

You can choose to export a match in PGN format. When you do, Android's sharing features or a local file-saving option may pass the export to an app or destination you select. That sharing is initiated and controlled by you; the privacy practices of the selected app or destination are governed by its own provider.

## 3. Advertising and third-party services

Chess Duel is free to play and contains no advertisements. It does not integrate advertising networks, analytics SDKs, or cloud-hosting services for game data. We do not sell or share personal information collected through the app because we do not collect such information.

## 4. Permissions

The app does not require access to your camera, microphone, contacts, or location to play chess. Android may display system-level prompts or notices for functions you choose to use, such as saving or sharing an exported PGN file.

## 5. Children's privacy

Chess Duel does not knowingly collect personal information from children or other users. Since the app does not collect personal information, it is not designed to build profiles of children. Parents or guardians who have questions can contact the developer using the details below.

## 6. Changes to this policy

If the app's data practices change, this policy will be updated to reflect those changes. The **Last updated** date above will also be revised. Please review this page periodically for the latest information.

## 7. Contact

For questions or feedback about this Privacy Policy, contact:

